    {
      "claim": "Cephalexin, a beta-lactam with a similar cephem core, showed measurable Caco-2 permeability of 8.42 x 10^-7 cm/s, indicating beta-lactam scaffolds can be absorbed, partly through carrier-mediated transport.",
      "card_ids": ["C49"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Atenolol, a low-permeability Caco-2 marker with Papp around 4 to 8 x 10^-7 cm/s and PAMPA below detection, has human oral bioavailability of about 50% to 63%, showing low in vitro permeability does not imply F below 20%.",
